OL,3,GNEWSAJudge ruled children could have
OL,4,A'life-saving' treatment after parents
OL,5,Arefused
OL,6,
OL,7,FA judge gave doctors permission to give
OL,8,F"potentially life-saving" medical
OL,9,Ftreatment to three children whose
OL,10,Fparents refused to give consent.
OL,12,FTwo boys were from Jehovah's Witness
OL,13,Ffamilies who opposed blood transfusions
OL,14,Fon religious grounds. One was being
OL,15,Ftreated for brain cancer and the other
OL,16,Fhad a blocked kidney.
OL,18,FThe parents of the third child refused
OL,19,Fa tetanus jab for their daughter, who
OL,20,Fwas bitten by the family dog, because
OL,21,Fthey "disputed the medical science"
OL,22,Fbehind it.
OL,23,APub: 20-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
